    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, but the core of our production hinges on two primary matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the way with an elite 81.87 efficiency score, benefiting from a massive +19% SP skill boost against R. V\u00e1squez and a favorable +16% park factor. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a high-upside play at 75.26, as he squares off against Gibson; the 5.87 xERA provides a clear runway for **Jackson Merrill** to produce counting stats. We are also leaning heavily into **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.33) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.05), both of whom capitalize on platoon advantages and strong lineup placement to anchor our quest for stolen bases and run production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Nolan Schanuel** out of the starting nine. With a score of 44.13, he cleared our \"Below Floor\" threshold, but ultimately lacked the ceiling of our starters due to a neutral platoon matchup and a tougher-than-average SP skill challenge from Jax. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding the performance of **Sam Antonacci** (48.56) and **Wade Meckler** (41.07); both are facing top-tier arms in Yamamoto and Jax, respectively, necessitating a tight monitoring of their at-bats as we manage our daily game caps. \n\nRisk management is paramount today, particularly with **Josh Jung** (50.86), who carries a warning due to a negative BvP history and a challenging matchup against Suarez. While **Liam Hicks** (54.07) and **Nasim Nunez** (50.40) provide stability at the bottom of the order, their scores remain firmly in the \"Marginal\" bucket. We are keeping **Luis Robert Jr.** on the shelf as he continues his recovery on the IL, while keeping a close eye on the late-day updates to ensure none of our middle-of-the-pack starters are skipped by late lineup changes.",
